  "scope": "Terminal input retry receipts, control revisions, delayed-key fences and explicit child-to-parent ownership handoff. Intermediate local-team evidence, not milestone or release completion.",
  "gitBase": "1839271dfeec89773428e1ebc5c1627ffc1a9a8a",
  "workingTree": true,
  "backendSHA256": "c30f222ba659b2135075ee69e11a6d6bbd3e4857ad6f54abddea06cbfc793f70",
  "distributionReady": false,
  "implemented": [
    "Latest identical input retries return a bounded cached receipt without another PTY write; expired/conflicting/out-of-order identities are rejected.",
    "Control revision and original frame input epoch fence delayed writes across human takeover, terminal transfer, chat changes and pane hiding.",
    "Uncertain input closes its process, returns an unknown outcome, and prevents a child from claiming completion; UI discards queued keys instead of resending. Lost Ctrl-C responses also pause input.",
    "Child or human can explicitly transfer a running child terminal to its pinned parent. Prepared/applied journal binds immutable ownership; retries return the original receipt. Original lifetime and request reservation remain in force.",
    "Child cleanup rechecks exact owner under the ownership lock, preserving transferred servers. Human transfer atomically queues a reserved notice to the child with the applied receipt.",
    "A real HTTP server survives child completion, is read/tested by its parent, dies on Stop all and is not replayed after reconnect. Both agent and human UI handoff paths pass."
  ],
